## Summary

**Changed:** `scripts/append_terminal_state_events.py` — 11 lines added at lines 751-765.

**What changed:** Added a `_status_source_map` dict that maps RunCompleted `status` values to `(source, class)` tuples, and conditionally adds `source` and `class` fields to the retroactive `FailureObserved` payload when there's a match.

**Mapping:**
| status | source | class |
|---|---|---|
| reverted | task_revert | verification |
| timeout | timeout | infrastructure |
| build_failure | build | code |
| test_failure | test | code |

Unknown statuses (no match in the map) produce no `source`/`class` fields — backward compatible with the renderer's `"-"` fallback.

**Verification:**
• ✅ `python3 -c "import ast; ast.parse(...); print('syntax ok')"` — syntax ok
• ✅ `python3 scripts/append_terminal_state_events.py --help` — runs and shows usage
• ✅ `grep -n 'source\|class' ... | grep -i 'failure\|fo\|observed'` — confirms new fields at lines 763, 765 near `payload_fo`

**Expected evidence:** Next `yyds state why last-failure` for a retroactive FailureObserved (from a reverted/timeout/build_failure/test_failure run) will show `source=task_revert`, `source=timeout`, `source=build`, or `source=test` instead of `source="-"`.

